Z||000015||Monkeyman||12-02-2000||04:28 PM||||I wouldn't say that Fieros and MR2 are related.  Maybe the MR2 was a foriegn exchange student who went to the same school as we did?  While I'll admit that there are some interesting similarities, the Fiero is <I>still</I> the only American made, mass produced (ha--now you can't include Deloreans, etc) mid engined, 2 seater sports car. <P>I don't have a problem with you MR2 guys hanging around as long as you don't start any wars or start to flame our beloved Plastic Fantastics.  I hate to admit it, but I actually looked at an MR2 once (same body style as the one that looks like 007Dougs Fiero).  Just a little too buzzy for me.  I've always loved Fieros and I'll never become a traitor.<P>That said, I would like to welcome all of the MR2ers to the greatest forum (of any kind) in the world.  You guys (gals?) will soon learn that I tend to get cranky when I think that there's a chance that my beloved Fiero might get bashed.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">Welcome, all! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
