Z||000017||VelociFero||12-02-2000||04:29 PM||||Funny how even the RX7 guys throw that "unreliable" insult around...<BR>They of all people should know it's all in how well you take care of your baby!<P>BTW, this is not a flame; I love 7s, especially the FDs.  Look closely at my Deuce's wheels...<P>------------------<BR>1991 2.2L MR2<BR>1986 GT Fiero <BR>00 Mustang (Black)<BR>00 Mustang (Silver)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.mr2pages.com/members/velocifero/SmallMR2one.jpg"> ||||reg||12
Z||000018||ur2biteme||12-02-2000||06:51 PM||||once upon a time, in a time not to long ago (back in '98) i was looking for a car.  i was either gonna get a 1st gen MR2 or a fiero.  well, 2 cars came around.  the fiero i'm driving now, and either an 85 or an 87 MR2.  both were stripped models.  i checked out the MR2 first (guy was firm at $2500 on it at a lot) my first impression was that it was too cramped.  WAY too small.  i still like the fact that the E-brake was in a more traditional location though.  everything was layed out in good locations for me, but it was too cramped.  the engine compartment looked the same to me.  the car was in good shape. just didnt seem to be "me".<P>next was my fiero.  i allready knew a good bit about them because my mom owned a new '88 way back when.  i checked out the '87 i've got now.  it wasnt in the best of conditions (the body damage mentioned in my signature) stereo looked like it was ripped out, tired steering rack, etc.  got in and fired her up.  that's when my decision was made.  this car has the most legroom of any car i've ever driven.  it has a feel of a car that was built way after '87, to me at least.  lol.  needless to say i wasnt leaving the lot without it.  <P>i guess i'm going against the grain here, but i like the look of the 1st gens, and happen to see more broken down fieros than i do of 1st gen MR2's, but i dont see nearly as many MR2s on the road.  almost like a 5 or 6 to 1 ratio.  my opinion on the second gens, well, may not sound pretty to some.  i like the look of them because they look like a blatent ripoff of the '86-'88 GT.  of course with some slightly different styling cues.  all in all i like both cars, and if i were to buy a newer car right now, i'd be looking real closely to the newer MR2 (i think the MR Spyder is ugly as sin), but if rumor holds true, i'll be buying a 2003 fiero.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>at any rate, welcome mr2 guys!  sorry about the bandwidth.<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>170k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
